      choices: ["The Gregorian calendar has 365 days, which is one day longer than the Hanke-Henry permanent calendar.", "Adopting the Hanke-Henry permanent calendar would help solve a problem with the Gregorian calendar.", "Designed so calendar dates would occur on the same day of the week each year, the Hanke-Henry calendar supports more predictable scheduling than does the Gregorian calendar.", "The Hanke-Henry permanent calendar was developed as an alternative to the Gregorian calendar, which is currently the most-used calendar in the world."],
